{%- comment -%}
  cx-buybox-core — the ENTIRE buy-box widget (config resolution, including
  the per-market preset lookup + all seven design presets + JSON island +
  noscript fallback), shared verbatim by:

    blocks/buy-box.liquid        the product-page app block (target: section)
    blocks/buy-box-embed.liquid  the app embed (target: body) for themes whose
                                 product section cannot take app blocks

  Both wrappers are thin: they pass their settings (or, for the embed, the
  section block's defaults) into this snippet, which renders the identical
  widget markup either way — same launch gating ([hidden][data-cellexia-gated]
  until cellexia.launch_status is "live"), same preview ribbon, same
  selling-plan wiring and JSON island consumed by assets/buy-box.js.

  NOTE FOR EDITORS: this comment deliberately contains NO Liquid tag or
  output delimiters. Liquid parses the body of a comment block even though it
  never renders it, so a half-written tag inside a comment can break the whole
  storefront page. Write tag names in prose (render / capture / assign), never
  as real tags.

  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║  THEME APP EXTENSION LIQUID RULES — READ BEFORE EDITING THIS FILE        ║
  ╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
  ║                                                                          ║
  ║  RULE 1 — NEVER "capture" THE OUTPUT OF A "render".                      ║
  ║  In a theme app extension Shopify wraps the output of EVERY render of    ║
  ║  an extension snippet in HTML comments:                                  ║
  ║      <!-- BEGIN app snippet: x -->…<!-- END app snippet -->              ║
  ║  Those markers are invisible when they land in MARKUP context, but as    ║
  ║  soon as the render is captured into a variable they become part of the  ║
  ║  STRING — and any later escape filter turns them into visible page text  ║
  ║  ("<!-- BEGIN app snippet: cx-design-text -->CHOOSE YOUR RITUAL…").      ║
  ║  That is exactly what corrupted the v1.2.0 storefront render.            ║
  ║  ⇒ A snippet may ONLY emit final markup. A snippet is never a function.  ║
  ║  ⇒ This file therefore contains ZERO render tags: every helper (text     ║
  ║    resolution, templating, frequency labels, save labels, price blocks,  ║
  ║    benefit list, reassurance, frequency control) is inlined below as     ║
  ║    liquid / assign blocks, or as a capture of PURE MARKUP.               ║
  ║  ⇒ The two block files each keep ONE render of cx-buybox-core. Its       ║
  ║    comment markers land in markup context (inside <body>, between        ║
  ║    elements) where they are ordinary invisible HTML comments. That is    ║
  ║    the only render allowed anywhere in this extension.                   ║
  ║                                                                          ║
  ║  RULE 2 — THE t FILTER RETURNS ALREADY-ESCAPED HTML. NEVER ESCAPE IT     ║
  ║  AGAIN. Shopify's translation filter returns escaped text: the locale    ║
  ║  string "Subscribe & Save" comes back as "Subscribe &amp; Save".         ║
  ║  Escaping that a second time yields "&amp;amp;", which renders as the    ║
  ║  literal characters "&amp;" on the page. See the contract below.         ║
  ║                                                                          ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  ══ STRING-SPACE CONTRACT (two spaces, never mixed) ═════════════════════════

  RAW  — unescaped source text, exactly as authored: merchant text from the
         cellexia.buybox_design JSON metafield, theme-editor block settings,
         Shopify object names (selling_plan.name). Variables carry the
         "_raw" suffix. RAW is what travels in data-cellexia-* attributes (single
         escape filter, which the browser decodes back to raw on
         getAttribute) and in the JSON island (single json filter, whose
         values buy-box.js writes with textContent).

  SAFE — HTML-escaped text, ready to be printed. Variables carry NO suffix.
         Printed with a plain output tag and NEVER filtered again.

  Conversions — each happens exactly once, at a marked boundary:
    RAW  → SAFE : the escape filter (the only escape in the pipeline)
    SAFE → RAW  : the documented un-escape chain in the "locale defaults"
                  block below. It is applied ONLY to t-filter output, which
                  is the one source that arrives pre-escaped, so that locale
                  defaults and merchant overrides can be resolved in ONE
                  space. "&amp;" is replaced LAST (otherwise "&amp;lt;"
                  would decode twice). escape(unescape(t)) == t, so this is
                  loss-free; and it stays correct in the hypothetical where
                  a future Shopify version stops escaping t output.

  Money — money + strip_html output is treated as SAFE (a shop's money_format
          may legitimately contain HTML entities: Shopify's own stock formats
          include "&pound;{{amount}}", "&euro;{{amount_with_comma_separator}}"
          and the widely used "{{amount}}&nbsp;CHF"; strip_html removes TAGS,
          never entities). It is therefore only ever injected into SAFE
          strings and NEVER escaped again — by any filter. Strings that MIX
          money with locale copy (the "then …", "Save …" and "… per delivery"
          lines) are consequently SAFE, and are un-escaped once on the way
          into the JSON island (where JS needs RAW).

          ISLAND EXCEPTION: money that enters the JSON island itself IS
          decoded SAFE → RAW there, exactly once, by the dedicated money
          chain (see the comment at the island's variants map). <script> is a
          raw-text element — the browser decodes entities in attributes and
          text nodes but NEVER inside the island — so leaving island money
          SAFE paints literal "&nbsp;"/"&euro;" through textContent and
          breaks the theme price sync's byte-for-byte text match.

  Named t-filter arguments are ONLY EVER inert placeholder literals
  ("{price}", "{amount}", "{frequency}") — never a real value. The t filter
  escapes whatever it interpolates, so passing it a SAFE money string would
  turn "&euro;" into "&amp;euro;", which prints as the literal characters
  "&euro;" on the page — the same visible-entity defect that corrupted the
  v1.2.0 render, one currency format away. (And in the mirror case where a
  future Shopify version stops escaping, a merchant-authored selling-plan
  name would reach the page unescaped instead. One placeholder rule is
  correct under BOTH behaviours.) "{" and "}" are untouched by every escape,
  so the placeholders survive the filter intact and the real values are
  substituted with `replace` immediately afterwards: SAFE values into the
  SAFE result that is printed, RAW values into the un-escaped copy that feeds
  the JSON island. Exactly one escape per value, on either path.

  data-cellexia-tpl — carries the RAW template so buy-box.js can re-resolve the
  percent/amount/frequency placeholders on variant/plan change and write the
  result with textContent. It is emitted ONLY when the RAW template actually
  contains a "{" placeholder (single exception, documented at its use site:
  a merchant-authored savingsTemplate is always emitted so the JS never
  overwrites it with the built-in "Save X" label).

  Params:
    render_context               'section' | 'embed'
    product                      the product object
    (There is no group-selection parameter. The selling plan group is resolved
    from the shop metafield allow-list and from nothing else — see the
    ownership block below.)
    uid                          unique id suffix (block.id) — input names,
                                 aria wiring, the scoped custom-css selector
    section_id                   section.id ('section' context only; the
                                 data-section-id attribute is omitted in the
                                 embed so buy-box.js falls back to a
                                 document-wide product-form lookup)
    shopify_attributes           block.shopify_attributes (theme editor)
    design_source                'app' or a forced preset key
    heading                      heading text ('' hides it)
    show_badge                   boolean
    badge_text                   badge override ('' → translated default)
    preselect_subscription       boolean
    show_frequency_selector      boolean (config layout.showFrequency, when
                                 published, wins in either direction)
    recommended_frequency_handle e.g. '8 weeks'
    savings_format               'percent' | 'absolute' | 'both'
    show_reassurance             boolean
    accent_color                 hex accent fallback when no published config
    compact_mode                 boolean

  GROUP OWNERSHIP (v1.2.4) — the widget renders OUR selling plan group or it
  renders NOTHING. A store may run more than one subscription app at the same
  time (cellexialabs.com also runs Joy Subscriptions, whose group offers 5%
  off), and every group on the product is a candidate as far as Liquid is
  concerned. The group this file picks decides the discount the page
  advertises AND the selling_plan id that reaches the cart, so picking a
  foreign group sells a competitor's plan through our widget and creates a
  contract that belongs to THAT app. The pick is therefore an allow-list, not
  a guess — see the ownership block at the top of the liquid block below.

  Frequency selector removal (v1.2.0): when the resolved show-frequency flag
  is false, NO dropdown/chips render in ANY preset — the planner degrades to
  a single recommended-cadence line ("Delivery every 8 weeks") — and the
  cart simply gets the default plan (recommended frequency, else the group's
  first plan), which is the id the nameless mirror below and the JSON
  island's "initialPlan" both carry.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product != blank and product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0 -%}

  {%- liquid
    # ══ OWNERSHIP — WHICH SELLING PLAN GROUP IS OURS ══════════════════════
    #
    # THE ONE RULE: render OUR group, or render NOTHING. Never a foreign one.
    #
    # The client's store runs a second subscription app (Joy Subscriptions,
    # 5% off) whose selling plan group sits FIRST on the product. This block
    # used to take that first group and then look for a group whose NAME
    # contains 'cellexia', so on that product it resolved to JOY's group: the
    # widget advertised Joy's discount and Joy's frequencies, the hidden
    # mirror and the cart injection carried a JOY selling plan id, and any
    # subscription created through our buy box became a Joy contract. Editing
    # our own plan changed nothing on the page, because our plan was never on
    # the page.
    #
    # The allow-list is the shop metafield cellexia.plan_groups (type json),
    # rewritten by the app on every plan sync (and again on go-live) and
    # defensively read here:
    #   {"v":1,"groupIds":["123","456"],"planIds":["789"]}
    # It may be absent (fresh install), blank, or hand-edited into any shape,
    # so nothing below assumes more than "maybe there is a list of ids".
    #
    # Ids are compared as STRINGS, one entry at a time, by EXACT equality.
    # Liquid hands out numeric ids and the metafield holds strings, so both
    # sides are normalised with an empty append. A substring test against a
    # joined list would let group 12 match an allow-listed 123 — which is how
    # a competitor's group gets rendered by accident.
    #
    # NO ALLOW-LIST, NO WIDGET. There is deliberately no other way to resolve
    # a group. An earlier build fell back to matching the group NAME against
    # the token 'cellexia' when the metafield was missing, and a name is
    # merchant-chosen text: on a store called Cellexia Labs, the OTHER app's
    # group can perfectly well be called "Cellexia Subscribe & Save", and that
    # fallback then rendered THEIR group — their discount on the page, their
    # selling plan id in the cart, their contract at the end of it. That is the
    # precise defect this block exists to make impossible, so the heuristic is
    # gone rather than narrowed: guessing from a name has no safe version.
    #
    # It costs nothing real. A product only carries OUR group once the plan has
    # been synced to Shopify, and syncing is what publishes the allow-list — so
    # "group on the product, no allow-list" is a transient failure state (a
    # metafield write that failed), not a normal one. In it the widget renders
    # nothing and leaves the admin-only marker below, the Preview & launch page
    # can republish, and re-syncing the plan from Plans fixes it for good.
    #
    # TWO FACTORS, NOT ONE, AND BOTH ARE MANDATORY: the group id must be
    # allow-listed AND the group must actually contain one of the allow-listed
    # PLAN ids. An allow-list carrying no plan ids at all therefore unlocks
    # nothing, on any product. Matching on
    # groupIds alone made this whole block only as trustworthy as one field of
    # one metafield: an allow-list naming the OTHER app's group id — a
    # hand-edit in Settings → Custom data, any app holding write_metafields, or
    # a bad group id persisted on a SellingPlanConfig — resolved cx_group to
    # JOY'S GROUP and the widget rendered it in full. Nothing downstream could
    # catch that, because everything downstream is documented to assume
    # "reaching this point means cx_group is OURS": Joy's selling plan id went
    # into the JSON island as initialPlan, into the hidden nameless mirror and
    # into the cart, and Joy's 5% became the price on our page. The plan ids in
    # the same metafield are independent evidence — they come from the plans WE
    # created through the Shopify API — so requiring both means one corrupted
    # or forged field cannot hand a competitor's group to the renderer.
    #
    # BOTH FACTORS ARE REQUIRED, ALWAYS. planIds used to be a VETO rather than
    # a requirement: when it was absent or empty the group-id match stood
    # alone. That was a hole, and not a theoretical one — it collapsed the two
    # factors back into one in precisely the state this app can emit itself.
    # publishOwnGroupsMetafield() writes {"groupIds":["77"],"planIds":[]}
    # whenever refreshOwnPlanIdsFromShopify() cannot read the group back (a
    # throttled or failed Shopify call), so "planIds is empty" is a state the
    # allow-list genuinely reaches. In it, ONE corrupt or forged field —
    # groupIds naming another app's group — put that group on the page in
    # full: its discount in the price, its selling plan id in the cart mirror
    # and in the JSON island, its contract at the end of it. The rendered
    # proof is in tests/liquid/two-apps.test.ts (Joy's 5% at CHF 60.80).
    #
    # The old reasoning was that failing closed here would take the buy box off
    # every product of a shop upgrading from a build that never recorded
    # SellingPlanConfig.shopifyPlanIds. That cost is real but it is the SAME
    # cost this file already accepts one screen up for a missing allow-list,
    # and it is the cheaper of the two failures by a wide margin: a widget that
    # is briefly absent sells nothing, while a widget showing a competitor's
    # plan sells THEIR subscription through our buy box and hands them the
    # contract. It is also transient by construction — publishing repairs the
    # plan ids before every write, and any plan sync from the Plans page
    # restores them — whereas a wrong render is silent and permanent.
    #
    # So an allow-list with no plan ids now unlocks NOTHING, exactly like an
    # allow-list with no group ids. Two independent fields must agree before a
    # single group is rendered, which is what makes "forge one field" stop
    # being enough.
    assign cx_allow = shop.metafields.cellexia.plan_groups.value
    assign cx_allow_ids = cx_allow.groupIds
    assign cx_allow_count = cx_allow_ids | size
    assign cx_allow_plan_ids = cx_allow.planIds
    assign cx_allow_plan_count = cx_allow_plan_ids | size
    assign cx_group = false
    assign cx_group_found = false

    if cx_allow_count > 0 and cx_allow_plan_count > 0
      for cx_g in product.selling_plan_groups
        assign cx_g_id = cx_g.id | append: ''
        assign cx_id_match = false
        for cx_allowed in cx_allow_ids
          assign cx_allowed_id = cx_allowed | append: ''
          if cx_allowed_id == cx_g_id
            assign cx_id_match = true
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if cx_id_match
          # Second factor. Scanning the group's own plans (rather than the
          # product's) keeps the question exactly "is THIS group one we built".
          # No `else` branch: cx_allow_plan_count is guaranteed > 0 by the
          # condition on the loop above, and if that ever stops being true the
          # flag stays false and nothing renders. There is deliberately no way
          # to reach a render with cx_plan_match defaulted to true.
          assign cx_plan_match = false
          for cx_p in cx_g.selling_plans
            assign cx_p_id = cx_p.id | append: ''
            for cx_allowed_plan in cx_allow_plan_ids
              assign cx_allowed_plan_id = cx_allowed_plan | append: ''
              if cx_allowed_plan_id == cx_p_id
                assign cx_plan_match = true
                break
              endif
            endfor
            if cx_plan_match
              break
            endif
          endfor

          # A group that fails the second factor is skipped, not fatal: keep
          # scanning, since a later group on the product may be genuinely ours.
          if cx_plan_match
            assign cx_group = cx_g
            assign cx_group_found = true
            break
          endif
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  -%}

  {%- if cx_group_found -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Everything from here to the matching else branch is the widget itself,
    left at its original indentation on purpose: the markup below is
    whitespace-sensitive (the byte-stable snapshot pins it, and several
    conditional attributes carry their own newline), so the ownership branch
    wraps it without re-indenting a single line.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- liquid
    # ── Launch gate: hidden for everyone until the app has gone live ───────
    # The metafield drop exposes .value; the default fallback also covers a
    # legacy raw-string access. Missing metafield => not live (fail closed).
    assign cx_launch_status = shop.metafields.cellexia.launch_status.value | default: shop.metafields.cellexia.launch_status
    assign cx_live = false
    if cx_launch_status == 'live'
      assign cx_live = true
    endif

    # ── Design config (published by the app's Buy box designer) ────────────
    assign cx_cfg = shop.metafields.cellexia.buybox_design.value
    assign cx_source = design_source | default: 'app'
    assign cx_preset = 'classic'
    assign cx_use_cfg = false
    assign cx_known_presets = 'classic toggle tiles inline value_stack planner subscription_max' | split: ' '
    if cx_source != blank and cx_source != 'app'
      assign cx_preset = cx_source
    elsif cx_cfg and cx_cfg.preset
      assign cx_preset = cx_cfg.preset
      assign cx_use_cfg = true
      # ── Per-market preset (config.markets, v1.6.0) ────────────────────────
      # The designer can pick a preset PER SHOPIFY MARKET, keyed by market
      # HANDLE, everything else (text, layout, style, behavior) inheriting the
      # base config. Every access is nil-safe: older stores and the test
      # harness may not expose localization.market at all, config.markets is a
      # v1.6.0 field older revisions lack, and a stored handle may name a
      # market that no longer exists. The lookup is an EXACT key match on the
      # handle string, and an entry naming an unknown preset falls back to the
      # BASE preset (never to a half-applied one). The forced design_source
      # branch above never reaches this code: the emergency override in the
      # theme editor wins over the whole published config, markets included.
      assign cx_market_handle = ''
      if localization.market.handle != blank
        assign cx_market_handle = localization.market.handle | append: ''
      endif
      if cx_market_handle != blank and cx_cfg.markets
        assign cx_market_entry = cx_cfg.markets[cx_market_handle]
        if cx_market_entry and cx_market_entry.preset != blank
          assign cx_market_preset = cx_market_entry.preset | append: ''
          if cx_known_presets contains cx_market_preset
            assign cx_preset = cx_market_preset
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endif
    unless cx_known_presets contains cx_preset
      assign cx_preset = 'classic'
    endunless

    # ── The selling plan group ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Resolved by the ownership block above, from the allow-list metafield and
    # nothing else. Reaching this point at all means cx_group is OURS.
    assign cx_multi_plan = false
    if cx_group.selling_plans.size > 1
      assign cx_multi_plan = true
    endif

    # ── Pick the preselected plan (recommended frequency, else first) ──────
    assign cx_selected_plan = cx_group.selling_plans | first
    assign cx_rec = recommended_frequency_handle | strip | downcase
    if cx_rec != blank
      assign cx_rec_found = false
      for p in cx_group.selling_plans
        unless cx_rec_found
          assign p_hay = p.name | downcase
          for opt in p.options
            assign opt_val = opt.value | downcase
            assign p_hay = p_hay | append: ' ' | append: opt_val
          endfor
          if p_hay contains cx_rec
            assign cx_selected_plan = p
            assign cx_rec_found = true
          endif
        endunless
      endfor
    endif
    # The recommended plan keeps its tag (planner) even if the allocation
    # fallback below moves the initial selection to another plan.
    assign cx_rec_plan_id = cx_selected_plan.id

    # ── Current variant (honours ?variant= deep links) ─────────────────────
    assign cx_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    if cx_variant == blank
      assign cx_variant = product.variants | first
    endif

    # ── Allocation for current variant + selected plan (with fallback) ─────
    assign cx_alloc = false
    for a in cx_variant.selling_plan_allocations
      if a.selling_plan.id == cx_selected_plan.id
        assign cx_alloc = a
        break
      endif
    endfor
    unless cx_alloc
      for a in cx_variant.selling_plan_allocations
        if a.selling_plan_group_id == cx_group.id
          assign cx_alloc = a
          assign cx_selected_plan = a.selling_plan
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endunless

    # ── Initial prices ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    if cx_alloc
      assign cx_first = cx_alloc.price
      assign cx_adj_count = cx_alloc.price_adjustments | size
      if cx_adj_count > 1
        assign cx_last_adj = cx_alloc.price_adjustments | last
        assign cx_ongoing = cx_last_adj.price
      else
        assign cx_ongoing = cx_alloc.price
      endif
      # An allocation with no per_delivery_price (nil, not 0) falls back to the
      # charge price, exactly like buy-box.js does for every later variant /
      # plan change (it reads plan.pd and falls back to plan.first). Without
      # the fallback the tiles and planner rows print the money filter's
      # rendering of nil next to a real price. Blank and not "greater than
      # zero": a genuinely free product has per_delivery_price 0, which is a
      # real value.
      # NOTE FOR EDITORS: no pipe characters in these comments — the harness
      # fidelity lint reads every "pipe word" in the file as a filter name.
      assign cx_pd_cents = cx_alloc.per_delivery_price
      if cx_pd_cents == blank
        assign cx_pd_cents = cx_first
      endif
    else
      assign cx_first = cx_variant.price
      assign cx_ongoing = cx_variant.price
      assign cx_pd_cents = cx_variant.price
    endif

    # ── Layout knobs (defaults = the v1.0.0 rendering / block settings) ────
    assign cx_order = 'sub_first'
    assign cx_density_compact = compact_mode
    assign cx_freq_style = 'dropdown'
    assign cx_show_badge = show_badge
    assign cx_show_savings = true
    assign cx_show_pd = true
    assign cx_show_compare = false
    assign cx_show_reassurance = show_reassurance
    assign cx_show_benefits = false
    assign cx_benefit_count = 4
    assign cx_show_freq = show_frequency_selector
    # subscription_max preset defaults (v1.6.0): quiet by design. The badge and
    # the frequency selector are OFF unless the merchant explicitly turns them
    # on — the config block below reads showBadge and showFrequency in BOTH
    # directions, so an explicit true still re-enables either. With the
    # selector off the plan default cadence is used, exactly like the
    # showFrequency=false path in every other preset.
    if cx_preset == 'subscription_max'
      assign cx_show_badge = false
      assign cx_show_freq = false
    endif
    if cx_use_cfg and cx_cfg.layout
      assign cx_l = cx_cfg.layout
      if cx_l.order == 'one_time_first'
        assign cx_order = 'one_time_first'
      endif
      if cx_l.density == 'compact'
        assign cx_density_compact = true
      elsif cx_l.density == 'comfortable'
        assign cx_density_compact = false
      endif
      if cx_l.frequencyStyle == 'chips'
        assign cx_freq_style = 'chips'
      endif
      # v1.2.0 — remove the frequency selector entirely (all six presets).
      # Read defensively: pre-v1.2.0 configs have no showFrequency key, and a
      # missing key must mean "show" (the v1.1.0 behavior).
      if cx_l.showFrequency == false
        assign cx_show_freq = false
      elsif cx_l.showFrequency == true
        assign cx_show_freq = true
      endif
      if cx_l.showBadge == false
        assign cx_show_badge = false
      elsif cx_l.showBadge == true
        assign cx_show_badge = true
      endif
      if cx_l.showSavings == false
        assign cx_show_savings = false
      endif
      if cx_l.showPerDelivery == false
        assign cx_show_pd = false
      endif
      if cx_l.showCompareAt == true
        assign cx_show_compare = true
      endif
      if cx_l.showReassurance == false
        assign cx_show_reassurance = false
      elsif cx_l.showReassurance == true
        assign cx_show_reassurance = true
      endif
      if cx_l.showBenefits == true
        assign cx_show_benefits = true
      endif
      if cx_l.benefitCount != blank
        assign cx_benefit_count = cx_l.benefitCount
      endif
    endif
    # value_stack IS the benefit panel — its archetype always renders the list.
    if cx_preset == 'value_stack'
      assign cx_show_benefits = true
      if cx_benefit_count < 1
        assign cx_benefit_count = 4
      endif
    endif

    # The frequency control renders at all only when it is switched on AND
    # the group has more than one cadence to choose from (a single-plan group
    # never rendered a selector in any version).
    assign cx_freq_ui = false
    if cx_show_freq and cx_multi_plan
      assign cx_freq_ui = true
    endif
    # The planner sells the cadence, so it always uses chips and tags the
    # recommended plan; every other preset follows layout.frequencyStyle.
    assign cx_ctl_style = cx_freq_style
    assign cx_ctl_recommended = false
    if cx_preset == 'planner'
      assign cx_ctl_style = 'chips'
      assign cx_ctl_recommended = true
    endif

    # ── Behavior knobs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    assign cx_sub_checked = preselect_subscription
    assign cx_anim = true
    if cx_use_cfg and cx_cfg.behavior
      if cx_cfg.behavior.preselect == 'subscription'
        assign cx_sub_checked = true
      elsif cx_cfg.behavior.preselect == 'one_time'
        assign cx_sub_checked = false
      endif
      if cx_cfg.behavior.animation == false
        assign cx_anim = false
      endif
    endif
    if product.requires_selling_plan
      assign cx_sub_checked = true
    endif

    # ── Style knobs → CSS custom properties (scoped via the inline style) ──
    # "" color slots mean "inherit the v1.0.0 default" (see presets.ts).
    # The fallback is the brand near-black, identical to the --cx-accent
    # default in assets/buy-box.css, to the app embed's accent_color and to
    # DEFAULT_DESIGN_CONFIG.style.accent: the accent is ALWAYS emitted inline
    # (it wins over the stylesheet), so a wrong default here would repaint the
    # whole widget — card border, badge, radio dot, check icons, savings — in
    # a colour the brand does not use, on both the no-config install and the
    # "force a preset" emergency override (which discards cx_cfg.style).
    assign cx_accent = accent_color | default: '#1d1d1b'
    assign cx_accent_soft = ''
    assign cx_style_extra = ''
    assign cx_custom_css = ''
    if cx_use_cfg
      if cx_cfg.style.accent != blank
        assign cx_accent = cx_cfg.style.accent
      endif
      # NOT appended to cx_style_extra: --cx-accent-soft has ONE fixed slot in
      # the inline style (below), so the attribute never carries the property
      # twice. Two declarations would rely on last-wins, and any theme, CDN or
      # minifier that dedupes or reorders inline declarations would repaint the
      # subscription card with the wrong one. Mirrors buybox-preview.tsx:
      # bgTint when set, otherwise the accent at 7% alpha.
      if cx_cfg.style.bgTint != blank
        assign cx_accent_soft = cx_cfg.style.bgTint
      endif
      if cx_cfg.style.text != blank
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-text: ' | append: cx_cfg.style.text | append: ';'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.style.badgeBg != blank
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-badge-bg: ' | append: cx_cfg.style.badgeBg | append: ';'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.style.badgeText != blank
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-badge-text: ' | append: cx_cfg.style.badgeText | append: ';'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.style.accentText != blank
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-accent-text: ' | append: cx_cfg.style.accentText | append: ';'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.style.fontScale and cx_cfg.style.fontScale != 1
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-font-scale: ' | append: cx_cfg.style.fontScale | append: ';'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.layout.radiusPx != blank and cx_cfg.layout.radiusPx != 12
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-radius: ' | append: cx_cfg.layout.radiusPx | append: 'px;'
      endif
      if cx_cfg.layout.borderWidthPx != blank and cx_cfg.layout.borderWidthPx != 1
        assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | append: ' --cx-border-width: ' | append: cx_cfg.layout.borderWidthPx | append: 'px;'
      endif
      # Server-sanitized before publish (sanitizeCustomCss); the replaces and
      # the brace walk here are an idempotent belt-and-suspenders against
      # hand-edited metafields. The slice mirrors the server's 5000-char cap
      # so the walk below is bounded whatever the metafield holds.
      if cx_cfg.style.customCss != blank
        assign cx_custom_css = cx_cfg.style.customCss | slice: 0, 5000 | replace: '<', '' | replace: '>', '' | replace: 'javascript:', '' | replace: '@import', ''
        # BRACE CONTAINMENT (mirrors sanitizeCustomCss): the css is emitted
        # inside the wrapper rule below, so a right brace that is not closing
        # a brace opened INSIDE the css closes the wrapper itself and every
        # rule after it becomes unscoped, storefront-global CSS. Walk the
        # segments between right braces keeping a depth counter and drop the
        # css entirely the moment depth would go negative. The 'x' sentinel
        # keeps split from collapsing trailing separators, so segment count
        # is always close-count + 1 and only the last segment (never followed
        # by a right brace) is skipped.
        assign cx_css_probe = cx_custom_css | append: 'x'
        assign cx_css_segments = cx_css_probe | split: '}'
        assign cx_css_depth = 0
        for cx_css_segment in cx_css_segments
          unless forloop.last
            assign cx_css_opens = cx_css_segment | append: 'x' | split: '{' | size
            assign cx_css_depth = cx_css_depth | plus: cx_css_opens | minus: 2
            if cx_css_depth < 0
              assign cx_custom_css = ''
              break
            endif
          endunless
        endfor
      endif
    endif
    # The soft fill resolves to exactly one value: the merchant's bgTint when
    # set, otherwise the accent at 7% alpha (the v1.0.0 rendering).
    if cx_accent_soft == blank
      assign cx_accent_soft = cx_accent | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.07
    endif
    # strip_html + escape: the values are zod-validated hex/px before publish,
    # so neither filter changes a legitimate token — they only keep a
    # hand-edited metafield from breaking out of the style attribute.
    # color_modify returns its input UNCHANGED when it is not a valid colour,
    # so cx_accent_soft has to be escaped here too, not only cx_accent.
    assign cx_accent_soft = cx_accent_soft | strip_html | escape
    assign cx_style_extra = cx_style_extra | strip_html | escape

    # ══ SAFE → RAW: locale defaults ═══════════════════════════════════════
    # `| t` returns HTML-ESCAPED text (RULE 2). Every locale string that has
    # to be merged with merchant config text, travel in a data-cellexia-* attribute
    # or reach buy-box.js as RAW is un-escaped here — ONCE, at this single
    # boundary — so all downstream resolution happens in RAW space and each
    # value is escaped exactly once where it is printed.
    # NOTE: '&amp;' is replaced LAST; replacing it first would decode
    # "&amp;lt;" twice and resurrect markup.
    # Locale strings printed directly in markup below (purchase_options,
    # per_delivery, tile_savings, tile_flexibility, benefit_flexibility,
    # preview_mode, recommended_tag) never enter this pipeline: they are
    # already SAFE and are printed with a plain, unfiltered output tag.
    assign cx_lc_subscribe_raw = 'subscribe_save' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_subscribe_pct_raw = 'subscribe_save_percent' | t: percent: '{percent}' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_one_time_raw = 'one_time' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_one_time_short_raw = 'one_time_short' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_most_popular_raw = 'most_popular' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_reassurance_raw = 'reassurance' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_freq_label_raw = 'frequency_label' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_delivery_every_raw = 'delivery_every' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_weeks_raw = 'weeks' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_first_order_raw = 'first_order' | t | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_buy_once_raw = 'or_buy_once' | t: amount: '{amount}' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_buy_once_quiet_raw = 'or_buy_once_quiet' | t: amount: '{amount}' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    assign cx_lc_b1 = 'benefit_first_order' | t
    assign cx_lc_b2 = 'benefit_ongoing' | t
    assign cx_lc_b3 = 'benefit_milestone_gift' | t
    assign cx_lc_b4 = 'benefit_flexibility' | t
    assign cx_lc_benefits_joined = cx_lc_b1 | append: '||' | append: cx_lc_b2 | append: '||' | append: cx_lc_b3 | append: '||' | append: cx_lc_b4
    assign cx_lc_benefits_raw = cx_lc_benefits_joined | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
    # SAFE locale strings that are printed as-is (never merged, never escaped).
    assign cx_lc_per_delivery = 'per_delivery' | t
    assign cx_recommended_label = 'recommended_tag' | t

    # ── Frequency label for the SELECTED plan (was cx-freq-label) ──────────
    # Extract the week count from the plan's option values (preferred) or its
    # name, but only when the string actually mentions weeks — this avoids
    # mislabelling month-based plans. With no usable week count (or a count of
    # 1, where "1 weeks" would read badly) fall back to the raw plan name,
    # which Shopify serves already translated when storefront translations
    # exist. RAW in, RAW out: plan names and the un-escaped locale words.
    assign cx_fl_weeks = 0
    for cx_fl_opt in cx_selected_plan.options
      assign cx_fl_val = cx_fl_opt.value | downcase
      if cx_fl_val contains 'week'
        assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_val | split: ' ' | first | plus: 0
        if cx_fl_cand > 0
          assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
          break
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    if cx_fl_weeks == 0
      assign cx_fl_name = cx_selected_plan.name | downcase
      if cx_fl_name contains 'week'
        assign cx_fl_tokens = cx_fl_name | split: ' '
        for cx_fl_tok in cx_fl_tokens
          assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_tok | plus: 0
          if cx_fl_cand > 0
            assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endif
    endif
    if cx_fl_weeks > 1
      assign cx_freq_raw = cx_fl_weeks | append: ' ' | append: cx_lc_weeks_raw
      assign cx_freq_full_raw = cx_lc_delivery_every_raw | append: ' ' | append: cx_freq_raw
    else
      assign cx_freq_raw = cx_selected_plan.name
      assign cx_freq_full_raw = cx_selected_plan.name
    endif
    assign cx_freq = cx_freq_raw | escape
    assign cx_freq_full = cx_freq_full_raw | escape

    # ── Template values for {percent} / {amount} / {frequency} ─────────────
    # cx_pct is digits + '%' (identical in both spaces); cx_amount is money
    # (SAFE by the money rule); cx_freq is SAFE. All three are injected into
    # SAFE strings, i.e. AFTER the single `| escape` of the template.
    assign cx_save_cents = cx_variant.price | minus: cx_first
    assign cx_save_pct = 0
    if cx_save_cents > 0 and cx_variant.price > 0
      assign cx_save_pct = cx_save_cents | times: 100.0 | divided_by: cx_variant.price | round
    endif
    assign cx_pct = ''
    if cx_save_pct > 0
      assign cx_pct = cx_save_pct | append: '%'
    endif
    assign cx_amount = cx_variant.price | money | strip_html

    # ── "then {price} every {frequency}" (SAFE: contains money) ────────────
    # The t filter is asked for the LOCALE SENTENCE ONLY, with inert
    # placeholder literals; the real values go in afterwards (see the
    # named-argument rule in the header). cx_ongoing_fmt is SAFE money, whose
    # entities must survive untouched; cx_freq is the selling-plan label
    # escaped exactly once. Both land in the already-escaped t output, so the
    # whole line is SAFE and is printed with a plain, unfiltered output tag.
    assign cx_then = ''
    if cx_ongoing != cx_first
      assign cx_ongoing_fmt = cx_ongoing | money | strip_html
      assign cx_then = 'then_price' | t: price: '{price}', frequency: '{frequency}'
      assign cx_then = cx_then | replace: '{price}', cx_ongoing_fmt | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | strip
    endif

    # ── "Save X" for the current allocation (was cx-save-label; SAFE) ──────
    # Nothing is rendered without a positive saving, so callers can always
    # print it and hide empty output. A percentage that rounds below 1%
    # degrades to the absolute amount rather than showing "Save 0%".
    assign cx_savings_format = savings_format | default: 'percent'
    assign cx_save = ''
    if cx_alloc and cx_save_cents > 0 and cx_variant.price > 0
      assign cx_save_fmt = cx_savings_format
      if cx_save_pct < 1
        assign cx_save_fmt = 'absolute'
      endif
      assign cx_save_abs = cx_save_cents | money | strip_html
      if cx_save_fmt == 'absolute'
        assign cx_save_amt = cx_save_abs
      elsif cx_save_fmt == 'both'
        assign cx_save_amt = cx_save_abs | append: ' (' | append: cx_save_pct | append: '%)'
      else
        assign cx_save_amt = cx_save_pct | append: '%'
      endif
      # Placeholder in, SAFE money/percent substituted after — never through
      # the t filter, which would escape the money entities a second time.
      assign cx_save = 'save_amount' | t: amount: '{amount}'
      assign cx_save = cx_save | replace: '{amount}', cx_save_amt | strip
    endif

    # ── "{price} per delivery" (SAFE: contains money) ──────────────────────
    # Prepaid plans only: the line exists to explain that one charge covers
    # several deliveries, so it renders only when the allocation states a
    # per-delivery price that DIFFERS from the charge. The blank guard is
    # separate (nested, because Liquid evaluates `and` right to left and
    # cannot short-circuit): a nil per_delivery_price is "unknown", not "0",
    # and printing the money filter's rendering of nil followed by
    # "per delivery" states a price the shopper will not be charged.
    assign cx_pd = ''
    if cx_alloc
      assign cx_pd_alloc = cx_alloc.per_delivery_price
      if cx_pd_alloc != blank and cx_pd_alloc != cx_alloc.price
        assign cx_pd_money = cx_pd_alloc | money | strip_html
        assign cx_pd = cx_pd_money | append: ' ' | append: cx_lc_per_delivery
      endif
    endif

    # ── Theme add-to-cart price sync (v1.2.2) ─────────────────────────────
    # Most themes print the price INSIDE their own add-to-cart button
    # ("ADD TO CART - CHF 64.00"). That is the one-time price, so with the
    # subscription selected the widget says CHF 51.20 while the button the
    # shopper is about to click still says CHF 64.00. buy-box.js swaps the
    # money STRING inside that button's text nodes (never innerHTML, never a
    # re-render) and needs both strings formatted by the SAME money filter
    # the theme used — which is what these two attributes carry.
    #
    # SPACE: both are SAFE money. A shop's money_format may legitimately
    # contain entities ("{{amount}}&nbsp;CHF", "&euro;{{amount}}"), so they
    # are NEVER escaped: escaping would ship "&amp;nbsp;" and the JS would
    # then look for a string no button on the page contains. The one
    # character that could break out of the attribute is the double quote,
    # which is converted to its entity here — the browser decodes it back on
    # getAttribute, so what the JS compares is byte-identical to what the
    # theme printed. (money is preceded by strip_html everywhere in this
    # file, so tags cannot reach the attribute either.)
    #
    # Later variant/plan changes are re-synced from the JSON island, whose
    # "oneTime" (per variant) and "first" (per variant x plan) keys are these
    # same two strings — no new island shape, and the JS still never formats
    # money.
    assign cx_money_onetime = cx_amount | replace: '"', '&quot;'
    assign cx_money_sub = ''
    if cx_alloc
      assign cx_money_sub = cx_first | money | strip_html | replace: '"', '&quot;'
    endif
    # Feature flag + optional theme-specific selector (design config
    # themeSync, published by the Buy box designer). Read defensively: a
    # pre-v1.2.2 config has no themeSync key, and a missing key means ON —
    # the swap only ever fires when the theme's button literally contains the
    # one-time money string AND the shopper selected the subscription, so it
    # is a no-op on themes whose button shows no price.
    assign cx_price_sync = true
    assign cx_price_selector_raw = ''
    if cx_use_cfg and cx_cfg.themeSync
      if cx_cfg.themeSync.syncAddToCartPrice == false
        assign cx_price_sync = false
      endif
      # Server-sanitized before publish (sanitizePlacementSelector); the
      # replaces are an idempotent belt against a hand-edited metafield.
      assign cx_price_selector_raw = cx_cfg.themeSync.priceSelector | default: '' | replace: '<', '' | replace: '>', '' | replace: '"', '' | replace: "'", '' | strip
    endif

    # ══ Config text lookup tables (locale → en → default) ═════════════════
    assign cx_t_loc = false
    assign cx_t_en = false
    if cx_use_cfg and cx_cfg.text
      assign cx_t_loc = cx_cfg.text[request.locale.iso_code]
      assign cx_t_en = cx_cfg.text['en']
    endif

    # ══ Text resolution (was cx-design-text + cx-tpl), key by key ═════════
    # Per key, in RAW space:  config.text[locale] → config.text.en → default.
    # Blank/whitespace-only overrides are treated as ABSENT so an empty admin
    # field can never blank out storefront copy.
    # Then, in ONE step: `| escape` (RAW → SAFE) + placeholder injection with
    # the already-SAFE values + whitespace collapse — so "Subscribe & save
    # {percent}" with no saving degrades cleanly to "Subscribe & save".

    # heading — default is the theme-editor block setting (already RAW).
    assign cx_heading_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_heading_raw = cx_t_loc.heading | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_heading_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_heading_raw = cx_t_en.heading | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_heading_raw == blank and cx_preset != 'subscription_max'
      # subscription_max skips the block-setting fallback on purpose: no
      # "choose your option" framing — its heading DEFAULTS to empty. A config
      # text override above still wins, in that preset like any other.
      assign cx_heading_raw = heading | default: ''
    endif
    assign cx_heading = cx_heading_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # subheading — config-only (no locale default).
    assign cx_subheading_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_subheading_raw = cx_t_loc.subheading | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_subheading_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_subheading_raw = cx_t_en.subheading | default: '' | strip
    endif
    assign cx_subheading = cx_subheading_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # badge — config → block setting → translated "Most popular".
    assign cx_badge_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_badge_raw = cx_t_loc.badge | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_badge_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_badge_raw = cx_t_en.badge | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_badge_raw == blank
      assign cx_badge_raw = badge_text | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_badge_raw == blank
      assign cx_badge_raw = cx_lc_most_popular_raw
    endif
    assign cx_badge = cx_badge_raw | escape

    # subscribeLabel — the toggle/inline default embeds {percent}.
    if cx_preset == 'toggle' or cx_preset == 'inline'
      assign cx_sub_label_default_raw = cx_lc_subscribe_pct_raw
    else
      assign cx_sub_label_default_raw = cx_lc_subscribe_raw
    endif
    assign cx_sub_label_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_sub_label_raw = cx_t_loc.subscribeLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_sub_label_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_sub_label_raw = cx_t_en.subscribeLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_sub_label_raw == blank
      assign cx_sub_label_raw = cx_sub_label_default_raw
    endif
    assign cx_sub_label = cx_sub_label_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # oneTimeLabel — full label, plus the short variant used by the toggle
    # tabs (one override key, two locale defaults — v1.1.0 behaviour).
    assign cx_onetime_override_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_onetime_override_raw = cx_t_loc.oneTimeLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_onetime_override_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_onetime_override_raw = cx_t_en.oneTimeLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    assign cx_onetime_label_raw = cx_onetime_override_raw
    if cx_onetime_label_raw == blank
      assign cx_onetime_label_raw = cx_lc_one_time_raw
    endif
    assign cx_onetime_short_raw = cx_onetime_override_raw
    if cx_onetime_short_raw == blank
      assign cx_onetime_short_raw = cx_lc_one_time_short_raw
    endif
    assign cx_onetime_label = cx_onetime_label_raw | escape
    assign cx_onetime_label_short = cx_onetime_short_raw | escape

    # savingsTemplate — config-only; when set it REPLACES the built-in
    # "Save X" copy (but only while there is a real saving to claim).
    assign cx_save_tpl_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_save_tpl_raw = cx_t_loc.savingsTemplate | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_save_tpl_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_save_tpl_raw = cx_t_en.savingsTemplate | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_save != blank and cx_save_tpl_raw != blank
      assign cx_save = cx_save_tpl_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip
    endif

    # reassurance
    assign cx_reassurance_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_reassurance_raw = cx_t_loc.reassurance | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_reassurance_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_reassurance_raw = cx_t_en.reassurance | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_reassurance_raw == blank
      assign cx_reassurance_raw = cx_lc_reassurance_raw
    endif
    assign cx_reassurance = cx_reassurance_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # frequencyLabel — the planner asks a question, the others label a select.
    if cx_preset == 'planner'
      assign cx_freq_label_default_raw = cx_lc_freq_label_raw
    else
      assign cx_freq_label_default_raw = cx_lc_delivery_every_raw
    endif
    assign cx_freq_label_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_freq_label_raw = cx_t_loc.frequencyLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_freq_label_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_freq_label_raw = cx_t_en.frequencyLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_freq_label_raw == blank
      assign cx_freq_label_raw = cx_freq_label_default_raw
    endif
    assign cx_freq_label = cx_freq_label_raw | escape

    # firstOrderLine
    assign cx_first_line_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_first_line_raw = cx_t_loc.firstOrderLine | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_first_line_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_first_line_raw = cx_t_en.firstOrderLine | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_first_line_raw == blank
      assign cx_first_line_raw = cx_lc_first_order_raw
    endif
    assign cx_first_line = cx_first_line_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # oneTimeLinkLabel — the value_stack escape hatch ("or buy once for X"),
    # and subscription_max's quiet demoted line (its own locale key, same
    # config override). The default copy embeds {amount} so the one-time
    # price is visible in the link BEFORE it is selected — the compliance
    # guardrail that keeps "quiet" from ever meaning "hidden".
    if cx_preset == 'subscription_max'
      assign cx_onetime_link_default_raw = cx_lc_buy_once_quiet_raw
    else
      assign cx_onetime_link_default_raw = cx_lc_buy_once_raw
    endif
    assign cx_onetime_link_raw = ''
    if cx_t_loc
      assign cx_onetime_link_raw = cx_t_loc.oneTimeLinkLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_onetime_link_raw == blank and cx_t_en
      assign cx_onetime_link_raw = cx_t_en.oneTimeLinkLabel | default: '' | strip
    endif
    if cx_onetime_link_raw == blank
      assign cx_onetime_link_raw = cx_onetime_link_default_raw
    endif
    assign cx_onetime_link = cx_onetime_link_raw | escape | replace: '{percent}', cx_pct | replace: '{amount}', cx_amount | replace: '{frequency}', cx_freq | replace: '  ', ' ' | strip

    # benefits — config array (RAW) → the four un-escaped locale defaults.
    assign cx_benefits_arr = false
    if cx_show_benefits
      if cx_t_loc and cx_t_loc.benefits.size > 0
        assign cx_benefits_arr = cx_t_loc.benefits
      elsif cx_t_en and cx_t_en.benefits.size > 0
        assign cx_benefits_arr = cx_t_en.benefits
      else
        assign cx_benefits_arr = cx_lc_benefits_raw | split: '||'
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ══ Shared markup fragments ═════════════════════════════════════════════
    These capture blocks contain PURE MARKUP — no render tag anywhere
    (RULE 1) — so printing them emits exactly what was captured. Liquid
    output tags do not escape, which is why captured markup round-trips
    unchanged; the strings inside them are already SAFE.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} Frequency control — dropdown or chips (was cx-freq-control) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign cx_freq_control = '' -%}
  {%- if cx_freq_ui -%}
    {%- capture cx_freq_control -%}
      {%- if cx_ctl_style == 'chips' -%}
        <fieldset class="cx-buybox__chips">
          <legend class="cx-buybox__sr">{{ cx_freq_label }}</legend>
          {%- for p in cx_group.selling_plans -%}
            {%- liquid
              # cx-freq-label (inlined) — see the selected-plan copy above.
              assign cx_fl_weeks = 0
              for cx_fl_opt in p.options
                assign cx_fl_val = cx_fl_opt.value | downcase
                if cx_fl_val contains 'week'
                  assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_val | split: ' ' | first | plus: 0
                  if cx_fl_cand > 0
                    assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
                    break
                  endif
                endif
              endfor
              if cx_fl_weeks == 0
                assign cx_fl_name = p.name | downcase
                if cx_fl_name contains 'week'
                  assign cx_fl_tokens = cx_fl_name | split: ' '
                  for cx_fl_tok in cx_fl_tokens
                    assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_tok | plus: 0
                    if cx_fl_cand > 0
                      assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor
                endif
              endif
              if cx_fl_weeks > 1
                assign cx_chip_raw = cx_fl_weeks | append: ' ' | append: cx_lc_weeks_raw
              else
                assign cx_chip_raw = p.name
              endif
              assign cx_chip_label = cx_chip_raw | escape
            -%}
            <label class="cx-buybox__chip">
              <input
                type="radio"
                class="cx-buybox__sr-input"
                name="cx-freq-{{ uid }}"
                value="{{ p.id }}"
                data-cellexia-freq-chip
                {% if p.id == cx_selected_plan.id %}checked{% endif %}
              >
              <span class="cx-buybox__chip-label">
                {{- cx_chip_label -}}
                {%- if cx_ctl_recommended and p.id == cx_rec_plan_id and cx_recommended_label != blank -%}
                  <span class="cx-buybox__chip-tag">{{ cx_recommended_label }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </label>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </fieldset>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__freq">
          <label class="cx-buybox__sr" for="cx-freq-{{ uid }}">{{ cx_freq_label }}</label>
          <select id="cx-freq-{{ uid }}" class="cx-buybox__freq-select" data-cellexia-freq>
            {%- for p in cx_group.selling_plans -%}
              {%- liquid
                # cx-freq-label (inlined), 'select' variant: full sentence.
                assign cx_fl_weeks = 0
                for cx_fl_opt in p.options
                  assign cx_fl_val = cx_fl_opt.value | downcase
                  if cx_fl_val contains 'week'
                    assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_val | split: ' ' | first | plus: 0
                    if cx_fl_cand > 0
                      assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
                      break
                    endif
                  endif
                endfor
                if cx_fl_weeks == 0
                  assign cx_fl_name = p.name | downcase
                  if cx_fl_name contains 'week'
                    assign cx_fl_tokens = cx_fl_name | split: ' '
                    for cx_fl_tok in cx_fl_tokens
                      assign cx_fl_cand = cx_fl_tok | plus: 0
                      if cx_fl_cand > 0
                        assign cx_fl_weeks = cx_fl_cand
                        break
                      endif
                    endfor
                  endif
                endif
                if cx_fl_weeks > 1
                  assign cx_opt_raw = cx_fl_weeks | append: ' ' | append: cx_lc_weeks_raw
                  assign cx_opt_raw = cx_lc_delivery_every_raw | append: ' ' | append: cx_opt_raw
                else
                  assign cx_opt_raw = p.name
                endif
                assign cx_opt_label = cx_opt_raw | escape
              -%}
              <option value="{{ p.id }}" {% if p.id == cx_selected_plan.id %}selected{% endif %}>
                {{- cx_opt_label -}}
              </option>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </select>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Benefit list (was cx-benefit-list) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign cx_benefits_html = '' -%}
  {%- if cx_benefits_arr and cx_benefit_count > 0 -%}
    {%- capture cx_benefits_html -%}
      <ul class="cx-buybox__benefits" role="list">
        {%- for b in cx_benefits_arr limit: cx_benefit_count -%}
          {%- assign cx_b_raw = b | strip -%}
          {%- if cx_b_raw != blank -%}
            <li class="cx-buybox__benefit">
              <svg class="cx-buybox__check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <path d="M6.5 11.3 3.4 8.2l1-1 2.1 2 5-5.1 1 1z" fill="currentColor"/>
              </svg>
              {{ cx_b_raw | escape }}
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Reassurance line (was cx-reassurance) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign cx_reassurance_html = '' -%}
  {%- if cx_reassurance != blank -%}
    {%- capture cx_reassurance_html -%}
      <p class="cx-buybox__reassurance">
        <svg class="cx-buybox__check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M6.5 11.3 3.4 8.2l1-1 2.1 2 5-5.1 1 1z" fill="currentColor"/>
        </svg>
        {{- cx_reassurance -}}
      </p>
    {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Subscription price cluster (was cx-sub-price-block + cx-price): big
    first-order price (optionally with the struck one-time compare-at), the
    "First order" microcopy, the "then …" line and the per-delivery line.
    Two variants: with the per-delivery row (classic / toggle / value_stack,
    honouring layout.showPerDelivery) and without it (tiles, which shows the
    per-delivery price in its own compare row instead).
    All data-cellexia-* hooks match buy-box.js: data-cellexia-sub-price,
    data-cellexia-first-label, data-cellexia-then, data-cellexia-per-delivery, data-cellexia-compare.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture cx_price_block -%}
    <span class="cx-buybox__price-row">
      <span class="cx-buybox__price cx-buybox__price--lg" data-cellexia-sub-price{% if cx_show_compare %} data-cellexia-compare{% endif %}>
        <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_first | money }}</span>
        {%- if cx_show_compare and cx_variant.price > cx_first %} <s class="cx-price__compare">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</s>{% endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="cx-buybox__first-label" data-cellexia-first-label{% if cx_first_line_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_first_line_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_first_line }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="cx-buybox__then" data-cellexia-then {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_then }}</span>
    {%- if cx_show_pd -%}
      <span class="cx-buybox__per-delivery" data-cellexia-per-delivery {% if cx_pd == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_pd }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture cx_price_block_nopd -%}
    <span class="cx-buybox__price-row">
      <span class="cx-buybox__price cx-buybox__price--lg" data-cellexia-sub-price{% if cx_show_compare %} data-cellexia-compare{% endif %}>
        <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_first | money }}</span>
        {%- if cx_show_compare and cx_variant.price > cx_first %} <s class="cx-price__compare">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</s>{% endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="cx-buybox__first-label" data-cellexia-first-label{% if cx_first_line_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_first_line_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_first_line }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="cx-buybox__then" data-cellexia-then {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_then }}</span>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    THE WIDGET ROOT. Its data-cellexia-money-* / data-cellexia-price-* attributes drive
    the theme add-to-cart price sync (see the assigns above): the two money
    strings for the CURRENT variant and plan, the on/off flag and the
    merchant's optional selector. data-cellexia-money-sub is empty when the current
    variant has no allocation in the group — there is no subscription price
    to promise, and buy-box.js then leaves the theme alone.

    Note on its class list: cx-buybox--no-sub means the
    variant the page opens on has NO allocation in this selling-plan group,
    so there is no subscription to sell for it (the CSS then hides every
    subscription-only fragment). buy-box.js toggles the same class on every
    variant change; emitting it here means the FIRST paint is honest too,
    instead of showing a subscription card priced at the one-time price
    until the JS runs.

    On the whitespace control below: a conditional attribute must never leave
    a whitespace-only line behind when its condition is false (that blank slot
    is harmless to browsers but shows up as noise in every byte-stable
    snapshot diff). Each conditional attribute below therefore opens with a
    LEFT-TRIMMING tag delimiter — a percent-brace opener carrying a hyphen —
    which eats the newline plus indentation that precedes it, and it then
    re-supplies that newline and indentation INSIDE its own body, ahead of the
    attribute. So the attribute is still written on its own line when the
    condition holds, and nothing at all is emitted when it does not. The
    separating newline always travels with the attribute it introduces, which
    is what keeps two attributes from gluing together (id="…"class="…").
    Never trim the trailing side of these tags, and never hoist that leading
    newline out of the body — either change re-creates one of the two bugs.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    id="cx-buybox-{{ uid }}"
    class="cx-buybox cx-buybox--{{ cx_preset }}{% if cx_density_compact %} cx-buybox--compact{% endif %}{% unless cx_anim %} cx-buybox--no-anim{% endunless %}{% unless cx_alloc %} cx-buybox--no-sub{% endunless %}"
    data-cellexia-buybox
    data-cellexia-preset="{{ cx_preset }}"
    data-block-id="{{ uid }}"
    data-cellexia-money-onetime="{{ cx_money_onetime }}"
    data-cellexia-money-sub="{{ cx_money_sub }}"
    data-cellexia-price-sync="{% if cx_price_sync %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
    data-cellexia-price-selector="{{ cx_price_selector_raw | escape }}"
    {%- if render_context == 'section' %}
    data-section-id="{{ section_id }}"{% endif %}
    {%- unless cx_live %}
    hidden data-cellexia-gated="true"{% endunless %}
    style="--cx-accent: {{ cx_accent | escape }}; --cx-accent-soft: {{ cx_accent_soft }};{{ cx_style_extra }}"
    {{ shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {%- if cx_custom_css != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Merchant custom CSS, sanitized server-side (sanitizeCustomCss) and
        scoped to this widget instance via CSS nesting under the wrapper id.
        The scoping is real only because BOTH sanitizer and the belt above
        enforce brace containment: css whose brace depth ever goes negative
        is dropped whole, so no right brace can close this wrapper rule and
        leak global CSS onto the storefront.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <style>#cx-buybox-{{ uid }} { {{ cx_custom_css }} }</style>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- unless cx_live -%}
      {%- comment -%} Shown only after buy-box.js validates a signed preview token. {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="cx-buybox__preview-ribbon" data-cellexia-preview-ribbon hidden>{{ 'preview_mode' | t }}</p>
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- if cx_heading != blank -%}
      <h3 class="cx-buybox__heading">{{ cx_heading }}</h3>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if cx_subheading != blank -%}
      <p class="cx-buybox__subheading">{{ cx_subheading }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <span class="cx-buybox__sr" id="cx-buybox-label-{{ uid }}">{{ 'purchase_options' | t }}</span>

    {%- case cx_preset -%}

      {%- when 'toggle' -%}
        {%- comment -%} ══ TOGGLE — segmented pill tabs + detail panel ══ {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__group cx-buybox__group--toggle">
          {%- unless product.requires_selling_plan -%}
            {%- capture cx_tab_sub -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cx-buybox__tab{% if cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endif %}"
                role="tab"
                id="cx-tab-sub-{{ uid }}"
                aria-controls="cx-panel-sub-{{ uid }}"
                aria-selected="{% if cx_sub_checked %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                {% unless cx_sub_checked %}tabindex="-1"{% endunless %}
                data-cellexia-tab="subscription"
              ><span class="cx-buybox__tab-label"{% if cx_sub_label_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_sub_label_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_sub_label }}</span></button>
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- capture cx_tab_one -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cx-buybox__tab{% unless cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endunless %}"
                role="tab"
                id="cx-tab-one-{{ uid }}"
                aria-controls="cx-panel-one-{{ uid }}"
                aria-selected="{% unless cx_sub_checked %}true{% else %}false{% endunless %}"
                {% if cx_sub_checked %}tabindex="-1"{% endif %}
                data-cellexia-tab="one_time"
              ><span class="cx-buybox__tab-label">{{ cx_onetime_label_short }}</span></button>
            {%- endcapture -%}
            <div class="cx-buybox__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ 'purchase_options' | t }}">
              {%- if cx_order == 'one_time_first' -%}{{ cx_tab_one }}{{ cx_tab_sub }}{%- else -%}{{ cx_tab_sub }}{{ cx_tab_one }}{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endunless -%}

          <div
            class="cx-buybox__panel cx-buybox__option--sub"
            role="tabpanel"
            id="cx-panel-sub-{{ uid }}"
            aria-labelledby="cx-tab-sub-{{ uid }}"
            data-cellexia-panel="subscription"
            {% unless cx_sub_checked %}hidden{% endunless %}
          >
            {%- if cx_show_savings -%}
              <span class="cx-buybox__save" data-cellexia-save{% if cx_save_tpl_raw != blank %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_save_tpl_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_save == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_save }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {{ cx_price_block }}
            {{ cx_freq_control }}
            {{ cx_benefits_html }}
            {%- if cx_show_reassurance -%}{{ cx_reassurance_html }}{%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- unless product.requires_selling_plan -%}
            <div
              class="cx-buybox__panel"
              role="tabpanel"
              id="cx-panel-one-{{ uid }}"
              aria-labelledby="cx-tab-one-{{ uid }}"
              data-cellexia-panel="one_time"
              {% if cx_sub_checked %}hidden{% endif %}
            >
              <span class="cx-buybox__title-row">
                <span class="cx-buybox__title">{{ cx_onetime_label }}</span>
                <span class="cx-buybox__price" data-cellexia-onetime-price>
                  <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>
          {%- endunless -%}
        </div>

      {%- when 'tiles' -%}
        {%- comment -%} ══ TILES — side-by-side comparison, subscription elevated ══ {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture cx_tile_sub -%}
          <div
            class="cx-buybox__option cx-buybox__tile cx-buybox__option--sub{% if cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endif %}"
            data-cellexia-option-wrap="subscription"
          >
            {%- if cx_show_badge and cx_badge != blank -%}
              <span class="cx-buybox__badge">{{ cx_badge }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <label class="cx-buybox__card cx-buybox__card--tile">
              <input
                type="radio"
                class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
                name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
                value="subscription"
                data-cellexia-option="subscription"
                {% if cx_sub_checked %}checked aria-checked="true"{% else %}aria-checked="false"{% endif %}
              >
              <span class="cx-buybox__card-body cx-buybox__card-body--stack">
                <span class="cx-buybox__card-main">
                  <span class="cx-buybox__title"{% if cx_sub_label_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_sub_label_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_sub_label }}</span>
                  {{ cx_price_block_nopd }}
                  <span class="cx-buybox__rows">
                    <span class="cx-buybox__row">
                      <span class="cx-buybox__row-label">{{ 'per_delivery' | t }}</span>
                      <span class="cx-buybox__row-value" data-cellexia-pd-price><span class="cx-price">{{ cx_pd_cents | money }}</span></span>
                    </span>
                    {%- if cx_show_savings -%}
                      <span class="cx-buybox__row" data-cellexia-save-row {% if cx_save == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>
                        <span class="cx-buybox__row-label">{{ 'tile_savings' | t }}</span>
                        <span class="cx-buybox__row-value cx-buybox__row-value--accent" data-cellexia-save{% if cx_save_tpl_raw != blank %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_save_tpl_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_save }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="cx-buybox__row">
                      <span class="cx-buybox__row-label">{{ 'tile_flexibility' | t }}</span>
                      <span class="cx-buybox__row-value">{{ 'benefit_flexibility' | t }}</span>
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </label>
            {{ cx_freq_control }}
            {{ cx_benefits_html }}
            {%- if cx_show_reassurance -%}{{ cx_reassurance_html }}{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- capture cx_tile_one -%}
          {%- unless product.requires_selling_plan -%}
            <div
              class="cx-buybox__option cx-buybox__tile{% unless cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endunless %}"
              data-cellexia-option-wrap="one_time"
            >
              <label class="cx-buybox__card cx-buybox__card--tile">
                <input
                  type="radio"
                  class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
                  name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
                  value="one_time"
                  data-cellexia-option="one_time"
                  {% unless cx_sub_checked %}checked aria-checked="true"{% else %}aria-checked="false"{% endunless %}
                >
                <span class="cx-buybox__card-body cx-buybox__card-body--stack">
                  <span class="cx-buybox__card-main">
                    <span class="cx-buybox__title">{{ cx_onetime_label }}</span>
                    <span class="cx-buybox__price-row">
                      <span class="cx-buybox__price cx-buybox__price--lg" data-cellexia-onetime-price>
                        <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</span>
                      </span>
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </label>
            </div>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__group cx-buybox__tiles" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="cx-buybox-label-{{ uid }}">
          {%- if cx_order == 'one_time_first' -%}{{ cx_tile_one }}{{ cx_tile_sub }}{%- else -%}{{ cx_tile_sub }}{{ cx_tile_one }}{%- endif -%}
        </div>

      {%- when 'inline' -%}
        {%- comment -%} ══ INLINE — one checkbox row, near-zero visual weight ══ {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__group cx-buybox__group--inline">
          <label class="cx-buybox__inline-row{% if cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endif %}" data-cellexia-option-wrap="subscription">
            <input
              type="checkbox"
              class="cx-buybox__inline-box"
              data-cellexia-inline
              {% if cx_sub_checked %}checked{% endif %}
              {% if product.requires_selling_plan %}disabled{% endif %}
              aria-describedby="cx-inline-detail-{{ uid }}"
            >
            <span class="cx-buybox__inline-label"{% if cx_sub_label_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_sub_label_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_sub_label }}</span>
          </label>
          <div class="cx-buybox__inline-detail" id="cx-inline-detail-{{ uid }}" data-cellexia-panel="subscription" {% unless cx_sub_checked %}hidden{% endunless %}>
            <span class="cx-buybox__price-row">
              <span class="cx-buybox__price" data-cellexia-sub-price{% if cx_show_compare %} data-cellexia-compare{% endif %}>
                <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_first | money }}</span>
                {%- if cx_show_compare and cx_variant.price > cx_first %} <s class="cx-price__compare">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</s>{% endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="cx-buybox__first-label" data-cellexia-first-label{% if cx_first_line_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_first_line_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_first_line }}</span>
            </span>
            <span class="cx-buybox__then" data-cellexia-then {% if cx_then == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_then }}</span>
            {%- if cx_show_pd -%}
              <span class="cx-buybox__per-delivery" data-cellexia-per-delivery {% if cx_pd == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_pd }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {{ cx_freq_control }}
            {%- if cx_show_reassurance -%}{{ cx_reassurance_html }}{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>

      {%- when 'value_stack' -%}
        {%- comment -%} ══ VALUE STACK — benefit panel, one-time demoted to a link ══ {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__group cx-buybox__group--stack" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="cx-buybox-label-{{ uid }}">
          <div
            class="cx-buybox__option cx-buybox__option--sub cx-buybox__stack-panel{% if cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endif %}"
            data-cellexia-option-wrap="subscription"
          >
            {%- if cx_show_badge and cx_badge != blank -%}
              <span class="cx-buybox__badge">{{ cx_badge }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <label class="cx-buybox__card">
              <input
                type="radio"
                class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
                name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
