      {%- when 'subscription_max' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          ══ SUBSCRIPTION MAX — the subscription card IS the buy box ══
          One calm card (price, the "then …" line, savings kept quiet, the
          reassurance line prominent) and, BELOW it with generous whitespace,
          the one-time purchase demoted to a single muted underlined line.
          Quiet is NOT hidden: one-time stays a real radio in the same group
          (the sr-radio pattern every card preset uses), reachable in exactly
          ONE interaction, with its price printed in the link BEFORE
          selection. Selecting it swaps the line into a minimal selected
          state (small check, label, price) plus a switch-back line wired to
          the subscription radio through its for attribute, so BOTH flows run
          through the one existing radio machinery in buy-box.js — no tabs,
          no parallel state machine. The switch-back label is aria-hidden on
          purpose: it is a pointer convenience that duplicates the radio
          group, which screen readers and keyboards already operate directly
          (and hiding it keeps it out of the subscription radio's accessible
          name, which its for association would otherwise extend). This
          preset deliberately ignores layout.order: one-time sits below the
          card, always — that placement is the preset.
