              <span class="cx-buybox__card-body cx-buybox__card-body--stack">
                <span class="cx-buybox__card-main">
                  <span class="cx-buybox__title-row">
                    <span class="cx-buybox__title"{% if cx_sub_label_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_sub_label_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_sub_label }}</span>
                    {%- if cx_show_savings -%}
                      <span class="cx-buybox__save cx-buybox__save--quiet" data-cellexia-save{% if cx_save_tpl_raw != blank %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_save_tpl_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_save == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_save }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                  {{ cx_price_block }}
                </span>
              </span>
            </label>
            {{ cx_freq_control }}
            {%- if cx_show_reassurance -%}{{ cx_reassurance_html }}{%- endif -%}
            {{ cx_benefits_html }}
          </div>
          {%- unless product.requires_selling_plan -%}
            <div class="cx-buybox__submax-onetime{% unless cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endunless %}" data-cellexia-option-wrap="one_time">
              <label class="cx-buybox__submax-choice">
                <input
                  type="radio"
                  class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
                  name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
                  value="one_time"
                  data-cellexia-option="one_time"
                  {% unless cx_sub_checked %}checked aria-checked="true"{% else %}aria-checked="false"{% endunless %}
                >
                <span class="cx-buybox__submax-link"{% if cx_onetime_link_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_onetime_link_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_onetime_link }}</span>
                <span class="cx-buybox__submax-picked">
                  <svg class="cx-buybox__check" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M6.5 11.3 3.4 8.2l1-1 2.1 2 5-5.1 1 1z" fill="currentColor"/>
                  </svg>
                  <span class="cx-buybox__submax-picked-label">{{ cx_onetime_label }}</span>
                  <span class="cx-buybox__submax-picked-sep" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
                  <span class="cx-buybox__submax-picked-price" data-cellexia-onetime-price><span class="cx-price">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</span></span>
                </span>
              </label>
              <label class="cx-buybox__submax-switchback" for="cx-submax-sub-{{ uid }}" aria-hidden="true">{{ 'switch_back' | t }}</label>
            </div>
          {%- endunless -%}
        </div>

      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          ══ CLASSIC — the v1.0.0 stacked full-width option cards ══
          With no saved config this branch renders the v1.0.0 markup
          unchanged (the resolved variables collapse to the old values).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture cx_card_sub -%}
      <div
        class="cx-buybox__option cx-buybox__option--sub{% if cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endif %}"
        data-cellexia-option-wrap="subscription"
      >
        {%- if cx_show_badge and cx_badge != blank -%}
          <span class="cx-buybox__badge">{{ cx_badge }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        <label class="cx-buybox__card">
          <input
            type="radio"
            class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
            name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
            value="subscription"
            data-cellexia-option="subscription"
            {% if cx_sub_checked %}checked aria-checked="true"{% else %}aria-checked="false"{% endif %}
          >
          <span class="cx-buybox__card-body">
            <span class="cx-buybox__control" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="cx-buybox__card-main">
              <span class="cx-buybox__title-row">
                <span class="cx-buybox__title"{% if cx_sub_label_raw contains '{' %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_sub_label_raw | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ cx_sub_label }}</span>
                {%- if cx_show_savings -%}
                <span class="cx-buybox__save" data-cellexia-save{% if cx_save_tpl_raw != blank %} data-cellexia-tpl="{{ cx_save_tpl_raw | escape }}"{% endif %} {% if cx_save == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>{{ cx_save }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              {{ cx_price_block }}
            </span>
          </span>
        </label>

        {{ cx_freq_control }}

        {%- if cx_show_reassurance -%}{{ cx_reassurance_html }}{%- endif -%}

        {{ cx_benefits_html }}
      </div>
        {%- endcapture -%}
        {%- capture cx_card_one -%}
      {%- unless product.requires_selling_plan -%}
        <div
          class="cx-buybox__option cx-buybox__option--onetime{% unless cx_sub_checked %} is-selected{% endunless %}"
          data-cellexia-option-wrap="one_time"
        >
          <label class="cx-buybox__card">
            <input
              type="radio"
              class="cx-buybox__radio cx-buybox__sr-input"
              name="cx-purchase-{{ uid }}"
              value="one_time"
              data-cellexia-option="one_time"
              {% unless cx_sub_checked %}checked aria-checked="true"{% else %}aria-checked="false"{% endunless %}
            >
            <span class="cx-buybox__card-body">
              <span class="cx-buybox__control" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="cx-buybox__card-main">
                <span class="cx-buybox__title-row">
                  <span class="cx-buybox__title">{{ cx_onetime_label }}</span>
                  <span class="cx-buybox__price" data-cellexia-onetime-price>
                    <span class="cx-price">{{ cx_variant.price | money }}</span>
                  </span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>
      {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}
        <div class="cx-buybox__group" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="cx-buybox-label-{{ uid }}">
          {%- if cx_order == 'one_time_first' -%}{{ cx_card_one }}{{ cx_card_sub }}{%- else -%}{{ cx_card_sub }}{{ cx_card_one }}{%- endif -%}
        </div>

    {%- endcase -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Hidden selling-plan MIRROR — deliberately NAMELESS.

      It records the resolved plan id (recommended frequency, else the group's
      first plan — the same id the JSON island carries as "initialPlan") in the
      DOM before any script runs, mirroring the visible preselection exactly:
      empty while one-time is preselected.

      IT MUST NEVER CARRY name="selling_plan". This markup travels WITH the
      widget, and buy-box-embed.js can move the widget INSIDE the theme's
      <form action="/cart/add"> (heuristics 3 and 4). buy-box.js has by then
      already injected its own selling_plan input into that form, so a named
      mirror would make TWO selling_plan fields in one form — and Shopify's
      cart parser keeps the LAST duplicate, which is not the one buy-box.js
      keeps updating. A shopper switching to "One-time" would still get a
      subscription line. The name therefore belongs to exactly one field, the
      one buy-box.js owns and tags data-cellexia-plan-input.

      No-JS safety is strengthened by the same rule: with scripting off
      nothing here can reach the cart at all (and the <noscript> rule below
      hides the widget, so no unfulfillable promise is shown). The [hidden]
      attribute is belt and braces against a theme reset that re-displays
      hidden inputs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <input
      type="hidden"
      hidden
      value="{% if cx_sub_checked %}{{ cx_selected_plan.id }}{% endif %}"
      data-cellexia-selling-plan
    >

    {%- comment -%}
      JSON island: fully localized price strings per variant x selling plan.
      buy-box.js only swaps strings — it never formats money or builds copy.
      "freq" and "savePct" feed the client-side {frequency}/{percent}
      template re-resolution; "pd" feeds the per-delivery hooks.

      "oneTime" (per variant) and "first" (per variant x plan) are ALSO the
      pair the theme add-to-cart price sync swaps: they are the same two
      money strings the root carries as data-cellexia-money-onetime /
      data-cellexia-money-sub for the initial variant and plan, so a variant or
      frequency change re-syncs the theme's button from here without the JS
      ever formatting money.

      STRING SPACE: every string here is RAW, because buy-box.js writes them
      with textContent (which would print "&amp;" literally if they were
      SAFE) — and because <script> is a raw-text element, so the browser
      never decodes entities inside it (unlike attributes and ordinary text
      nodes). MONEY is therefore decoded to RAW at this boundary too, via the
      money chain documented at the variants map below: a SAFE money string
      here would surface "&nbsp;"/"&euro;" as literal characters in every
      price line and kill the theme price sync's text match. The composed
      strings (then / save / perDelivery) take their locale sentence through
      the same SAFE → RAW un-escape chain as the locale-defaults block above,
      and only THEN receive the plan label (RAW) and the RAW money string —
      so no value is ever escaped or un-escaped more than once.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="application/json" data-cellexia-data>
      {
        "initialVariant": "{{ cx_variant.id }}",
        "initialPlan": "{{ cx_selected_plan.id }}",
        "preselect": {% if cx_sub_checked %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
        "requiresSellingPlan": {% if product.requires_selling_plan %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
        "variants": {
          {%- for v in product.variants -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              MONEY SAFE → RAW (island boundary). <script> is a raw-text
              element: the browser never decodes entities inside it, unlike
              the data-cellexia-money-* attributes (decoded on getAttribute)
              and the theme's own text nodes (decoded at parse). So every
              money string entering the island is decoded HERE, exactly once:
              the money-format entities Shopify's stock formats actually use
              (&nbsp; &pound; &euro; &yen; &cent;) plus the standard
              un-escape set, &amp; LAST. Without this, a shop on
              "{{amount}}&nbsp;CHF" gets the literal characters "&nbsp;"
              painted into every price line by textContent, and the theme
              add-to-cart price sync never matches the button's parser-decoded
              text.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign v_onetime_raw = v.price | money | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&pound;', '£' | replace: '&euro;', '€' | replace: '&yen;', '¥' | replace: '&cent;', '¢' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&' -%}
            "{{ v.id }}": {
              "available": {% if v.available %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
              "oneTime": {{ v_onetime_raw | json }},
              "plans": {
                {%- assign cx_plan_i = 0 -%}
                {%- for a in v.selling_plan_allocations -%}
                  {%- if a.selling_plan_group_id == cx_group.id -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      # cx-freq-label (inlined) for this allocation's plan.
                      assign a_weeks = 0
                      for a_opt in a.selling_plan.options
                        assign a_opt_val = a_opt.value | downcase
                        if a_opt_val contains 'week'
                          assign a_cand = a_opt_val | split: ' ' | first | plus: 0
                          if a_cand > 0
                            assign a_weeks = a_cand
                            break
                          endif
                        endif
                      endfor
                      if a_weeks == 0
                        assign a_plan_name = a.selling_plan.name | downcase
                        if a_plan_name contains 'week'
                          assign a_tokens = a_plan_name | split: ' '
                          for a_tok in a_tokens
                            assign a_cand = a_tok | plus: 0
                            if a_cand > 0
                              assign a_weeks = a_cand
                              break
                            endif
                          endfor
                        endif
                      endif
                      if a_weeks > 1
                        assign a_freq_raw = a_weeks | append: ' ' | append: cx_lc_weeks_raw
                      else
                        assign a_freq_raw = a.selling_plan.name
                      endif

                      # "then {price} every {frequency}" — the locale sentence
                      # only (placeholder arguments, per the header rule),
                      # un-escaped ONCE to RAW, then the RAW plan label and
                      # the RAW money string substituted in. The money is
                      # decoded to RAW FIRST (the island-boundary money chain
                      # documented above the variants map): substituting a
                      # SAFE money into the already-un-escaped sentence would
                      # leave its "&nbsp;"/"&euro;" as literal characters,
                      # which textContent then paints on the page.
                      assign a_adj_count = a.price_adjustments | size
                      if a_adj_count > 1
                        assign a_last_adj = a.price_adjustments | last
                        assign a_ongoing = a_last_adj.price
                      else
                        assign a_ongoing = a.price
                      endif
                      assign a_then_raw = ''
                      if a_ongoing != a.price
                        assign a_ongoing_fmt = a_ongoing | money | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&pound;', '£' | replace: '&euro;', '€' | replace: '&yen;', '¥' | replace: '&cent;', '¢' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                        assign a_then = 'then_price' | t: price: '{price}', frequency: '{frequency}'
                        assign a_then_raw = a_then | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                        assign a_then_raw = a_then_raw | replace: '{price}', a_ongoing_fmt | replace: '{frequency}', a_freq_raw | strip
                      endif

                      # "Save X" (cx-save-label inlined) — locale sentence
                      # un-escaped to RAW, then the RAW amount substituted in
                      # (money decoded first — island-boundary money chain).
                      assign a_save_cents = v.price | minus: a.price
                      assign a_pct = 0
                      if a_save_cents > 0 and v.price > 0
                        assign a_pct = a_save_cents | times: 100.0 | divided_by: v.price | round
                      endif
                      assign a_pct_str = ''
                      if a_pct > 0
                        assign a_pct_str = a_pct | append: '%'
                      endif
                      assign a_save_raw = ''
                      if a_save_cents > 0 and v.price > 0
                        assign a_save_fmt = cx_savings_format
                        if a_pct < 1
                          assign a_save_fmt = 'absolute'
                        endif
                        assign a_save_abs = a_save_cents | money | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&pound;', '£' | replace: '&euro;', '€' | replace: '&yen;', '¥' | replace: '&cent;', '¢' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                        if a_save_fmt == 'absolute'
                          assign a_save_amt = a_save_abs
                        elsif a_save_fmt == 'both'
                          assign a_save_amt = a_save_abs | append: ' (' | append: a_pct | append: '%)'
                        else
                          assign a_save_amt = a_pct | append: '%'
                        endif
                        assign a_save = 'save_amount' | t: amount: '{amount}'
                        assign a_save_raw = a_save | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                        assign a_save_raw = a_save_raw | replace: '{amount}', a_save_amt | strip
                      endif

                      # "{price} per delivery" — the label is un-escaped to
                      # RAW on its own, THEN the RAW money (island-boundary
                      # money chain) is prepended. Composing BEFORE un-escaping
                      # would run the chain over the money too — decoding a
                      # legitimate money "&amp;" a second time and leaving
                      # "&nbsp;" untouched either way. Same two conditions as
                      # the initial render above: a per-delivery price that is
                      # stated (not nil) and that differs from the charge.
                      # a_pd_cents mirrors the JS fallback so the island never
                      # carries a "pd" the widget would refuse to believe.
                      assign a_pd_cents = a.per_delivery_price
                      if a_pd_cents == blank
                        assign a_pd_cents = a.price
                      endif
                      assign a_pd_money_raw = a_pd_cents | money | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&pound;', '£' | replace: '&euro;', '€' | replace: '&yen;', '¥' | replace: '&cent;', '¢' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                      assign a_pd_raw = ''
                      if a.per_delivery_price != blank and a.per_delivery_price != a.price
                        assign a_pd_label_raw = cx_lc_per_delivery | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                        assign a_pd_raw = a_pd_money_raw | append: ' ' | append: a_pd_label_raw | strip
                      endif

                      # "first" (and "oneTime" above) are the pair the theme
                      # add-to-cart price sync compares against parser-decoded
                      # button text — RAW via the same money chain.
                      assign a_first_raw = a.price | money | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&pound;', '£' | replace: '&euro;', '€' | replace: '&yen;', '¥' | replace: '&cent;', '¢' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&'
                    -%}
                    {%- if cx_plan_i > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
                    {%- assign cx_plan_i = cx_plan_i | plus: 1 -%}
                    "{{ a.selling_plan.id }}": {
                      "first": {{ a_first_raw | json }},
                      "then": {{ a_then_raw | json }},
                      "save": {{ a_save_raw | json }},
                      "perDelivery": {{ a_pd_raw | json }},
                      "pd": {{ a_pd_money_raw | json }},
                      "freq": {{ a_freq_raw | json }},
                      "savePct": {{ a_pct_str | json }}
                    }
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              }
            }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        }
      }
    </script>

    <noscript>
      {%- comment -%}
        Without JS the widget cannot write selling_plan into the product form;
        showing it would promise a subscription the cart would not contain.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <style>
        #cx-buybox-{{ uid }} .cx-buybox__group,
        #cx-buybox-{{ uid }} .cx-buybox__heading,
        #cx-buybox-{{ uid }} .cx-buybox__subheading { display: none; }
      </style>
    </noscript>
  </div>

  {%- else -%}{%- comment -%}
    ══ NO OWNED GROUP ON THIS PRODUCT ═══════════════════════════════════════

    The product carries selling plans, but none of them are ours: another
    subscription app owns every group on it. The widget renders NOTHING —
    the same output as a product with no selling plans at all. No wrapper,
    no JSON island, no style, no hidden input, nothing a shopper can see or
    a script can pick up as a widget.

    The single exception is the marker below, and it is not markup a shopper
    can ever perceive: a template element renders nothing by definition (its
    contents are not even in the document tree), it carries the hidden
    attribute as well, and it holds no text. It exists so that
    assets/buy-box.js can tell "this product has foreign plans and none of
    ours" apart from "this file did not run", and show the admin a
    diagnostic — but ONLY inside a server-validated preview session
    (CellexiaSubs.previewValidated, never the raw token). To a customer it is
    a zero-height, zero-content, invisible node.

    It deliberately carries none of the widget's own hooks: the class is
    cx-buybox-nogroup and the attribute data-cellexia-no-owned-group, so no
    selector in either asset file can mistake it for a widget or a wrapper.

    Three independent reasons it can never take part in layout, because the
    marker ships to a live storefront we do not control: the element type
    (a browser's default sheet hides template), the hidden attribute, and the
    inline declaration, which no theme stylesheet can outrank. A theme that
    re-displays hidden elements — some do, for accessibility hacks — would
    otherwise turn this into a zero-height block box, and a zero-height box
    is still a grid or flex ITEM in a buy column that uses one.
  {%- endcomment -%}<template class="cx-buybox-nogroup" data-cellexia-no-owned-group hidden style="display:none!important"></template>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- endif -%}
